archmage84 wrote:
> Is it just me, or is playing NetHack by hitting commands in time with
> some good music really fun? What are our opinions on music and
> NetHack?

I've observed that the "right" music can be relaxing when playing, but
playing the "wrong" music - which may even be my favourite ones - will
aid in killing me. The point is that I can play (or rather win) nethack
only if I am not too much distracted by the music (or whatever). Music
with a persistent rhythm can support confidence and fluent play; though,
playing Nethack successfully requires, IMO, that you adjust your playing
speed to the various situations. Having two "processes" (music and NH)
with non-synchronized "drive" can spoil a game. The consequence for me
is to play music while playing Nethack only if it's unobtrusive and in
the background.

